cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "IronMule: adaptive local LLM inference for GGUF and MLX"
message: "If you use IronMule or its measurements, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abenthum
    given-names: Tobias
    alias: Tobayko
    website: "https://github.com/Tobayko"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tobayko/IronMule"
abstract: >-
  IronMule is an OpenAI-compatible server for local language model inference
  with GGUF and MLX. Its Pilot is a decision model trained from scratch to
  schedule work on the available hardware. The runtime measures execution
  costs and evaluates changes in throughput, time to first token and answer
  quality. The project's benchmarks compare IronMule with llama.cpp and vLLM
  on documented hardware and workloads.
keywords:
  - MLX
  - GGUF
  - llama.cpp
  - OpenAI-compatible server
  - continuous batching
  - Apple silicon
  - NVIDIA CUDA
  - local LLM
  - LLM inference
  - inference runtime
  - KV cache
  - prefix caching
  - batching
  - reproducible research
license: "Apache-2.0"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-11"
